  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1214 AM CDT Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nA strong upper level trough and Pacific cold front will move east\nacross west central Texas late Monday afternoon and night. Expect\nscattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms to fire along the\nfront(Cam models showing this already) and move east across the \narea. Much of our area is in a marginal risk for severe so a low \nchance that a few storms may produce large hail and damaging \nwinds. Please keep up with the latest weather information as we \nare in the secondary severe weather season. A warm day Monday with\nhighs 80 to 85.\n\nLooks like a quiet weather pattern next week into the weekend as \nadditional storm systems are not expected until after the long \nterm period. Highs will be in the lower to mid 70s with overnight \nlows in the 40s to lower 50s.",
